ns make it austere in youth and magnificent with age and roast meats.","x":"284:2,285:85,286:82,287:48,288:60,289:70,290:75,291:30,292:0,293:30,2:75,6:55,9:45,7:30,14:30,26:20,198:45,186:40,185:25,148:35,151:30,143:25,114:30,111:25,120:20,72:15,216:70,220:30,230:50,239:55,245:80,242:70,258:60,278:75,260:55,279:45,282:85,296:100,297:100,299:100,295:100,310:100"},{"s":"donnhoff-oberhauser-leistenberg-riesling-kabinett","n":"Oberhäuser Leistenberg Riesling Kabinett","p":"Dönnhoff","t":"white","c":"Germany","r":"Nahe","a":"Oberhäuser Leistenberg","g":["Riesling"],"pr":32,"abv":9,"e":"Fermented and aged in stainless steel and traditional Stückfass","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–15 years","ds":"Nahe Kabinett at its most crystalline: white peach, pear and lime blossom drawn over the grey-slate cool of the Leistenberg. The sweetness reads as ripeness rather than sugar, carried off by a fine, chiming acidity and a long stony echo.","x":"284:35,285:85,286:0,287:15,288:25,289:65,290:72,291:2,292:3,293:15,53:60,46:55,35:50,49:40,57:35,55:25,40:35,85:40,86:30,139:80,136:60,140:35,158:15,191:8,228:55,229:60,230:50,254:60,249:80,236:75,240:85,243:80,258:70,260:30,282:60,279:75,296:100,308:100,305:100,323:100"},{"s":"jj-prum-wehlener-sonnenuhr-riesling-spatlese","n":"Wehlener Sonnenuhr Riesling Spätlese","p":"Joh. Jos. Prüm","t":"white","c":"Germany","r":"Mosel","a":"Wehlener Sonnenuhr","g":["Riesling"],"pr":70,"abv":8,"e":"Spontaneous fermentation in stainless steel and old Fuder; bottled early with a trace of CO2","sv":"8–10°C","d":"30 minutes when young to blow off the house''s reductive, struck-match sulfur","w":"5–40 years; often shut down in youth","ds":"The reference point for Mosel Spätlese: a famously reductive, matchstick-scented nose that opens into white peach, apricot and honeysuckle over blue slate. Sweetness and acidity are held in near-weightless balance, with a faint prickle in youth and a capacity to evolve for decades.","x":"284:50,285:90,286:0,287:10,28