ne treatment: green apple, lemon and lime threaded with brioche from extended lees ageing. The mousse is fine and persistent, the acidity laser-straight, making it a sharper, more aromatic alternative to non-vintage Champagne.","x":"284:8,285:85,286:0,287:38,288:30,289:55,290:60,291:2,292:90,293:20,46:70,34:55,35:50,53:40,49:30,36:25,85:35,178:35,180:25,181:30,136:45,139:25,141:15,233:75,228:80,225:35,240:90,249:60,236:55,256:60,272:90,266:40,279:70,283:60,323:100,306:100,319:100,307:100"},{"s":"domane-wachau-gruner-veltliner-federspiel-terrassen","n":"Grüner Veltliner Federspiel Terrassen","p":"Domäne Wachau","t":"white","c":"Austria","r":"Wachau","a":"Wachau DAC","g":["Grüner Veltliner"],"pr":18,"abv":12,"e":"Stainless steel","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–4 years","ds":"Textbook Federspiel from the Wachau''s terraced slopes: green apple, lemon and snap pea with the unmistakable white-pepper tickle of Grüner. Light on its feet and briskly dry, it is a do-everything white for the weeknight table.","x":"284:3,285:68,286:2,287:38,288:38,289:55,290:55,291:0,292:3,293:10,46:70,34:50,35:35,49:35,36:20,121:75,96:60,89:20,95:20,85:20,136:45,140:30,228:70,229:50,225:35,240:90,256:75,258:70,249:45,261:85,279:85,283:75,313:100,319:100,303:100,296:100"},{"s":"knoll-loibenberg-gruner-veltliner-smaragd","n":"Ried Loibenberg Grüner Veltliner Smaragd","p":"Weingut Knoll","t":"white","c":"Austria","r":"Wachau","a":"Wachau DAC, Ried Loibenberg","g":["Grüner Veltliner"],"pr":60,"abv":13.5,"e":"Stainless steel and large old oak casks","sv":"10–12°C","d":"30–60 minutes when young","w":"3–20 years","ds":"Smaragd-level ripeness from a steep primary-rock terrace: yellow apple, pear and quince seasoned heavily with white pepper and a whisper of tobacco leaf. Broad and almost creamy, yet it ends with a stony, peppery bite that promises long life in bottle.","x":"284:5,285:68,286:4,287:68,288:72,289:78,290:82,291:6,292:0,293:20,47:55,46:35,49:45,51:30,53:35,40:35,121:80,96:35,119:20