:"Burgenland","a":"Burgenland","g":["Zweigelt"],"pr":20,"abv":12.5,"e":"Spontaneous fermentation; brief ageing in large neutral casks","sv":"13–15°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–3 years","ds":"Austria''s everyday red done with care: sour cherry, raspberry and a sprinkle of black pepper in a supple, juicy frame. Lightly chilled, it has the gulpable charm of Beaujolais with a little more spice.","x":"284:3,285:62,286:32,287:40,288:38,289:55,290:50,291:8,292:0,293:12,2:75,1:55,3:40,9:35,7:25,16:15,120:40,122:20,71:20,151:15,229:75,231:50,212:30,228:35,240:85,244:65,256:85,265:25,260:40,279:85,283:85,301:100,296:100,311:100,302:100"},{"s":"royal-tokaji-aszu-5-puttonyos-red-label","n":"Tokaji Aszú 5 Puttonyos (Red Label)","p":"Royal Tokaji","t":"dessert","c":"Hungary","r":"Tokaj","a":"Tokaji Aszú","g":["Furmint","Hárslevelű","Muscat Blanc à Petits Grains"],"pr":55,"abv":11,"e":"Botrytised aszú berries macerated in base wine, then aged 2+ years in Hungarian oak in tufa cellars; 500ml bottle","sv":"9–11°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–30+ years","ds":"Noble rot in its most electric form: apricot, Seville marmalade, honey and saffron in a viscous, golden wine. What sets Tokaji apart from Sauternes is the volcanic-soil acidity that slices through the sugar and leaves the finish clean and endlessly long.","x":"284:85,285:88,286:3,287:20,288:75,289:88,290:92,291:30,292:0,293:30,55:75,32:65,210:75,39:50,31:40,51:40,58:25,59:20,192:80,209:85,132:25,129:30,124:15,206:25,171:20,204:15,193:25,223:65,229:45,238:75,257:75,255:85,248:75,258:85,240:50,269:95,260:50,282:95,280:35,322:100,317:100,320:100,308:100"},{"s":"oremus-mandolas-dry-furmint","n":"Mandolás Dry Furmint","p":"Oremus","t":"white","c":"Hungary","r":"Tokaj","a":"Tokaji","g":["Furmint"],"pr":30,"abv":13.5,"e":"Fermented and aged around 6 months in Hungarian oak barrels","sv":"10–12°C","d":"30 minutes","w":"Now–10 years","ds":"Tokaj''s great grape shown bone-dry: quince, yellow apple and lemon pith with a smoky, volcanic edge. Firm acidity and a light phenolic grip give it the frame of a serious white Burgundy with a more feral, mineral accent.","x":"284:4,285:82,286:4,287:58,288:60,289:70,290:75,291:30,292:0,293:18,51:60,47:50,49:45,34:45,35:30,45:30,53:30,55:20,79:15,158:40,146:50,136:40,141:30,137:25,202:20,192:15,157:20,156:10,232:25,224:35,230:55,245:60,243:65,242:35,248:55,259:25,260:35,282:65,279:60,296:100,298:100,303:100,312:100"},{"s":"domaine-sigalas-santorini-assyrtiko","n":"Santorini Assyrtiko","p":"Domaine Sigalas","t":"white","c":"Greece","r":"Santorini","a":"Santorini PDO","g":["Assyrtiko"],"pr":40,"abv":14,"e":"Stainless steel, several months on fine lees","sv":"9–11°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–10 years","ds":"Old, basket-trained vines on volcanic pumice give a white of startling salinity: lemon, lemon pith and crushed seashell over smoky, ashen stone. Powerful in alcohol yet bone-dry and racy, it finishes like a sea breeze.","x":"284:2,285:92,286:6,287:68,288:55,289:75,290:80,291:0,292:0,293:15,34:80,40:55,35:40,36:30,45:35,46:30,53:20,85:20,102:15,100:10,146:85,141:85,136:60,137:35,158:25,144:35,232:30,230:70,225:50,228:65,239:40,243:95,249:70,245:60,240:80,261:80,278:55,282:75,279:70,306:100,305:100,303:100,319:100"},{"s":"thymiopoulos-earth-and-sky-xinomavro-naoussa","n":"Earth & Sky (Gi kai Ouranos) Xinomavro","p":"Domaine Thymiopoulos","t":"red","c":"Greece","r":"Macedonia","a":"Naoussa PDO","g":["Xinomavro"],"pr":32,"abv":13.5,"e":"Aged in a mix of large casks and used barrels","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1 hour","w":"3–15 years","ds":"Greece''s answer to Nebbiolo: sour cherry and pomegranate with sun-dried tomato, black olive and dried herbs on a perfumed, rose-tinged nose. The tannins are firm and grippy, the acidity high, and the whole thing tastes savoury, sunlit and built to age.","x":"284:2,285:78,286:68,287:50,288:55,289:68,290:72,291:25,292:0,293:20,2:70,1:45,9:40,7:30,8:20,118:50,112:40,111:35,107:20,72:30,197:25,124:15,123:15,126:15,153:30,148:20,186:20,216:55,