,"ds":"Georgia''s inky teinturier grape made in clay: blackberry, black plum and mulberry with an iron-and-earth core and a grind of black pepper. Deeply coloured and chewy but kept fresh by Saperavi''s natural acidity.","x":"284:3,285:72,286:70,287:55,288:72,289:75,290:70,291:0,292:0,293:18,12:65,15:60,14:45,17:40,20:35,2:30,8:20,71:30,120:35,123:15,126:20,143:30,151:30,153:20,114:20,216:60,218:30,227:45,229:40,251:50,255:65,242:50,246:40,277:85,265:50,279:70,282:60,295:100,300:100,294:100,297:100"},{"s":"chateau-musar-rouge","n":"Château Musar Rouge","p":"Château Musar","t":"red","c":"Lebanon","r":"Bekaa Valley","a":"Bekaa Valley","g":["Cabernet Sauvignon","Cinsault","Carignan"],"pr":60,"abv":14,"e":"Varieties fermented separately in cement; about 12 months in French oak, then blended and further aged in cement and bottle; released around 7 years after vintage","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1 hour; often throws sediment","w":"Released at ~7 years; drinks 10–40+ years from vintage","ds":"A singular, gloriously idiosyncratic red: dried cherry, fig and fruitcake meet leather, cured meat and a brettish barnyard whiff. Released already mature, it is silky, spicy and savoury, with a volatile lift and a capacity to keep evolving for decades.","x":"284:3,285:68,286:55,287:60,288:60,289:78,290:82,291:30,292:0,293:65,26:65,9:40,2:35,23:30,22:35,30:30,124:25,123:25,135:30,159:30,155:40,185:55,188:35,189:25,186:35,197:30,199:25,148:30,212:40,214:30,231:40,248:85,253:55,242:65,246:35,258:70,267:30,265:45,260:50,281:60,282:95,295:100,297:100,310:100,315:100,299:100"},{"s":"movia-lunar-rebula","n":"Lunar Rebula","p":"Movia","t":"orange","c":"Slovenia","r":"Goriška Brda","a":"Goriška Brda","g":["Rebula (Ribolla Gialla)"],"pr":55,"abv":12.5,"e":"Whole berries left to ferment and macerate in barrique for around eight months, timed to the lunar calendar; settled by gravity, bottled unfiltered with no added sulfur","sv":"13–15°C","d":"Stand the bottle upright and decant off the sediment","w":"Now–12 years","ds":"Aleš Kristančič''s moon-timed Rebula is skin-contact wine at its most textural and alive: blood orange, dried apricot and quince with black tea, hazelnut and a cloudy, yeasty depth. Gentle tannin and bright acidity keep it fresher and more fruit-led than the long-aged Oslavia amber wines.","x":"284:2,285:70,286:40,287:45,288:58,289:75,290:78,291:15,292:0,293:25,32:55,55:40,39:60,38:35,51:50,33:30,41:25,114:45,79:30,116:25,192:30,203:35,202:25,129:25,111:20,181:25,141:25,136:20,232:80,227:30,229:45,242:60,248:70,253:35,240:60,264:100,265:95,260:50,280:35,282:65,296:100,298:100,310:100,315:100"},{"s":"gravner-ribolla-anfora","n":"Ribolla (Anfora)","p":"Gravner","t":"orange","c":"Italy","r":"Friuli-Venezia Giulia","a":"Venezia Giulia IGT (Oslavia)","g":["Ribolla Gialla"],"pr":120,"abv":14,"e":"Fermented and macerated around six months on skins in buried Georgian qvevri, then about six years in large oak; released roughly seven years after vintage","sv":"14–16°C","d":"1–2 hours","w":"Released at ~7 years; 10–30 years from vintage","ds":"Josko Gravner''s qvevri Ribolla is the amber wine against which all others are measured: dried apricot, quince and orange peel layered with honey, black tea, saffron and toasted nuts. Profound, tannic and saline, it has the gravity and slow unfolding of a great aged red.","x":"284:2,285:68,286:52,287:62,288:70,289:82,290:90,291:25,292:0,293:45,32:65,39:55,51:50,38:20,192:45,193:35,114:50,79:25,116:20,202:30,204:35,203:30,132:20,129:20,211:15,141:40,136:30,232:90,215:35,224:35,248:95,242:75,255:70,245:70,264:100,277:95,265:85,260:70,267:30,280:55,282:95,296:100,298:100,315:100,310:100"},{"s":"kozlovic-malvazija-istarska","n":"Malvazija Istarska","p":"Kozlović","t":"white","c":"Croatia","r":"Istria","a":"Hrvatska Istra","g":["Malvazija Istarska"],"pr":20,"abv":13,"e":"Stainless steel, a short time on fine lees","sv":"8–10°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–3 years","ds":"Istria''s signature white in its fresh, coastal guise: 